      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "b109bf80ecbccd32eb396a3336e3e8e3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"ai-audit\">AI Audit</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this notebook, we will use AI audit data to check for most common <code>robots.txt</code> violations.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Prerequisites:</strong><br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- API token (see <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/s3/tokens/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for info on how\n to create one);<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- at least one active zone with a <code>robots.txt</code> file.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><span style='color:tomato'>Note:</span> when making a GET request to the specified zone's robots.txt page,\nit is required that the domain returns the CORS <code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin</code> header.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "45dea4b2ca655e70776b252f21a11322",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"obtain-and-parse-robotstxt-rules\">Obtain and parse robots.txt rules</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">First, we will select the zone by its ID and fetch the associated hostname. On the GraphQL side, data is\nobtained by filtering by both ID and host. The hostname is also important to obtain since we must fetch\nand process the given zone's <code>robots.txt</code> manually.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "b110ed58d33861514e7dcb3f44a4244f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Now we will fetch and parse content found on the <code>/robots.txt</code> path, using the <code>urllib</code> library.</span>\n<div class=\"admonition attention\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Attention</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">It is not guaranteed that requesting <code>robots.txt</code> content will be successful, as requests using this method\nare perceived as bot traffic which may be blocked depending on how the zone is configured, as well as due to\nother factors.</span>\n</div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
